posted October 24, 2001 02:17 PM &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=get_profile&u=00000001" target=_blank>
<IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/profile_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Profile for Sleethr"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com" target=_new><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/homepage.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Author's Homepage"></A> &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000001"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/priv_message.gif" BORDER='0' ALT="Send New Private Message"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=edit_post&f=6&t=000010&reply_num=000002&u=00000001"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/edit_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Edit/Delete Post"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=reply&f=6&t=000010&replyto=000002"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/quote_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Reply With Quote"></A>
</FONT>
<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
From:  <A HREF="http://daoc.warcry.com/index.php/content/compendium/midgard/classes/menu/midgard" TARGET=_blank>http://daoc.warcry.com/index.php/content/compendium/midgard/classes/menu/midgard</A> <P><B>Viking </B><BR>=====================<BR><B>Warrior   ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>The standard Norse fighting man, the Warrior can use all weapons and armor, although he receives no spells. He more than makes up for it by his extreme ferocity and tenacity in battle. <P><B>Berserker  ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>Berserkers have the ability to drive themselves into a battle rage that lets them fight without thought of personal safety. At higher levels they can shapeshift into bears for additional power. <P><B>Thane   ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>The Thane is a fighter who can call up on weather-related magical direct-damage spells to aid him in combat.  <P><B>Skald   ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>Specializing in songs that instill courage and strength in his countrymen, the Skald is a tremendous boon to a party of adventurers. As dexterous as he is with a lute, the Skald is equally at home with a sword. <BR>  <BR><B>Mystic    </B><BR>=====================<BR><B>Runemaster  ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>Runemasters learn the arts of crafting magical runes which they use to create large area spells, traps, and explosions. <P><B>Spiritmaster  ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>Hel provides Spiritmasters the ability to summon and control the spirits of fallen Norse warriors to aid them in battle. <BR>  <BR><B>Seer    </B><BR>=====================<BR><B>Healer  ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>Healers are given knowledge of the arts of aiding their friends who have been injured in combat. Eir also provides Healers with some ability to fight as well. <P><B>Shaman   ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>Shamen are the tribal mages from the wild tribes of Kobolds and Trolls who draw their power from the earth itself. They get a combination of healing and combat magic that makes them quite useful to their realmmates. <BR>  <BR><B>Rogue    </B><BR>=====================<BR><B>Hunter   ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>Hunters are efficient fighters, who additionally get the ability to charm and control wild animals, as well as track and use bows. They can also shapeshift into animal form at higher levels. <P><B>Shadowblade   ( Norseman Dwarf Kobold Troll )</B><BR>The Shadowblade is a combination thief/illusionist, specializing in priestly abilities to sneak, hide, and confuse, as well as getting deadly combat abilities.<P><BR>Thought I'd post a quick and dirty class listing here for ya all to look at/reference as we go forward with these class discussions.<P>Right now...I'd caution against attempting to min/max the group and your character.  The game is too new as are we all to the game to worry about figuring out what we should spec in or not spec in as a caster.  We already have a lot of bases covered.  We have a healer/rezzer with Medec and Ghall.  We have a tank type with Wardak. We have sneaky rogue type with Bluhr and finally we have one of those mysterious magic user types.  I'm pretty sure we can hold our own rather well.<P>The only thing I'm a little concerned about is the crowd control part.  The Healer class also is the primary CC in Midgard and also being a primary healer that can be a tad busy.  <P>Having a Skald would kick butt too.  They are 75% warrior based, so having one of them would be like having another tank too.<P>Mostly...I would just like people to look at the classes and find one to play that they think sounds fun or interesting.  We can take things from there and build on it.<p>[ October 24, 2001: Message edited by: Sleethr ]<P>--------------------<P>Sleethr - 54th DE Mage<BR>Medec - 44th level Battle Cleric<BR>Meekka - 34th DE Rogue<BR>Vowk - 29th Dr00d
</FONT>
